        "target_node": "step1"
      },
      "teacher_script": "We start with the standard quadratic equation ax² + bx + c = 0. To derive the formula, we will complete the square. First, we divide the entire equation by 'a'.",
      "template_data": {
        "title": "Step-by-Step Derivation",
        "formula": "x² + (b/a)x + (c/a) = 0",
        "steps": [
          "Divide by a: x² + (b/a)x + (c/a) = 0",
          "Rearrange: x² + (b/a)x = - (c/a)",
          "Complete the square: (x + (b/2a))² = (b² - 4ac)/4a²",
          "Solve for x: x = -b ± √(b² - 4ac) / 2a"
        ]
      }
    },
